 "description": "COL-07, Kotlin + UI half. The native .cube parse + apply landed in the\ncore; this wires it end to end on the Android side: import, per-clip\nselection + Strength, preview, and export.\n\nData model:\n- GradeK gains lutId (String?, null = no LUT) and lutStrength (Float,\n  0..100 UI percent, default 100). Old project.json files parse the\n  missing fields as null/100 — no LUT selected, so the old look is\n  bit-identical.\n- The selection and the Strength are SEPARATE grade fields saved per\n  clip with the rest of the grade (owner request 2026-11-10 section 3).\n- LutStore: SAF import copies the .cube into the app-private luts dir as\n  <id>.cube, fingerprints the first 1 MiB + size (SHA-256, first 16\n  hex chars as the id) so the same file picked twice dedupes to one\n  entry. Entries live in the \"luts\" section of project.json; setTitle\n  applies the parsed TITLE rename; remove drops the entry and ",
